---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure"
  description="How DevToolPick handles affiliate links, sponsorships, and editorial independence."
>
  <div class="container prose">
    <h1>Affiliate &amp; advertising disclosure</h1>
    <p>
      Some links on DevToolPick may be affiliate links. If you click and purchase,
      we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you. This helps fund research and hosting.
    </p>
    <h2>Amazon Associates</h2>
    <p>DevToolPick is a participant in the Amazon Associates Program. As an Amazon Associate we earn from qualifying purchases.</p>
    <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
    <p>
      Affiliate relationships do not buy rankings. When we recommend a tool, it is because
      we believe it is a strong fit for the use case described. We will disclose sponsored posts separately if/when they exist.
    </p>
    <h2>A8.net (Japanese section)</h2>
    <p>
      Some Japanese articles contain affiliate links through A8.net. These links are marked <code>rel="nofollow sponsored"</code>
      and A8.net may load a 1×1 tracking image to attribute referrals. Official product pages remain the source of truth for pricing and features.
    </p>
    <h2 id="privacy">Analytics &amp; privacy</h2>
    <p>
      We count visits with <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/" rel="noopener">GoatCounter</a>, an open-source analytics service
      that sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and does not track you across sites. It records the page path, referrer, browser,
      screen size and country (from the IP address, which is not stored). We also count clicks on affiliate links and
      completions of the tool finder as anonymous events. We don't sell data or use it for advertising.
      Blocking the script (for example with an ad blocker) has no effect on how the site works.
    </p>
    <h2>Display ads</h2>
    <p>
      We may add privacy-respecting display ads later (for example Google AdSense) once traffic qualifies.
      Ads will never be presented as editorial recommendations.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
